&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years working in regulatory legal related to Internet regulation (e.g., user safety, minor safety, privacy, data protection, consumer protection)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of regulatory landscapes across UK/EU and/or Australia, including UK &amp;amp; Australian Online Safety Act and EU Digital Services Act.&amp;nbsp; Knowledge of GDPR, AI Act, privacy rights, data protection, consumer protection, and relevant industry standards is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience meeting with applicable regulators in one or more of the UK, EU and Australia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing and submitting responses to requests for information or other inquiries from relevant regulatory agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;License to practice law in a relevant jurisdiction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or for a company or companies in the social media, communication/ messaging, content or gaming spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing projects, prioritizing, and achieving results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively, independently, strategically, and with sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent emotional intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
